c QIF benchmark 2/7: 3-bit password equality to constant 5 (binary 101).
c
c Vars: 1=h1 (LSB), 2=h2, 3=h3 (MSB), 4=l (observable).
c Logic: l <-> (h3 AND NOT h2 AND h1). l=1 iff secret = 5.
c Models: 8 total. Of those, 1 has l=1 (h=5); 7 have l=0.
c Leakage on l=1: log2(8/1) = 3 bits; on l=0: log2(8/7) ~= 0.19 bits.
c Expected number of guesses to recover: 1 if l=1, ~4 if l=0.
c
c Reference: Heusser & Malacaria, "Quantifying Information Leaks in
c Software" (ACSAC 2010), Sec 4.1 — equality-to-constant channel.
p cnf 4 4
-4 3 0
-4 -2 0
-4 1 0
-3 2 -1 4 0
